<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-KRAJICEK PULLS OUT OF STOCKHOLM OPEN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-KRAJICEK PULLS OUT OF STOCKHOLM OPEN.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wimbledon champion Richard Krajicek pulled out of next week's $825,000 Stockholm tournament because of a knee injury, ATP Tour officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Dutchman, ranked seventh in the world, lost to Spain's Alberto Berasategui in the second round of the Paris Open on Tuesday and afterwards complained about stomach pains.</p>
</text>
